    "site_desc": "South Parlin forest is a young second-growth redwood forest located in the Jackson Demonstration State Forest near Fort Bragg, California. Jackson is the largest demonstration state forest managed by the Department of Forestry and Fire Protection, California (CAL FIRE), providing a unique living laboratory in a coastal redwood forest to study the effects of various forest management techniques. The forest regenerated after the second clearcut in 1988. The current dominant overstory vegetation are coast redwood. followed by Douglas fir. The site is situated on a northwest-southeast facing slope (20%).",
